body:
Coordinator: this PR was closed by GitHub at 20:23:41Z, not by a person. Its base branch `issue/3316-offset-pass-start` was deleted when the parent PR #3353 merged, and the PR was not retargeted first (AGENTS.md, "Overlapping issues stack").

I put it right:
- the base branch was restored at the head of #3353 (f2a03d947) for a moment;
- this PR is open again, with the same head `fc59bd583`;
- its base is now `main`, which contains #3353 (merge commit e313aa663);
- the temporary branch is deleted again.

No commit of this PR changed. The labels are as they were (`needs-rework`, `P3`, draft). @mkinney the stack is gone: the branch can take `git merge upstream/main` when you work on the review items.
